What is Radar Warning Receiver (RWR) for Rotorcraft?
Radar Warning Receivers (RWR) for rotorcraft are specialized electronic warfare systems designed to detect, identify, and locate radar emissions from hostile threats, providing critical situational awareness to helicopter crews. These systems enable pilots to recognize incoming radar-guided missiles, anti-aircraft artillery, and enemy aircraft, allowing timely deployment of countermeasures and evasive maneuvers. RWRs for rotorcraft typically feature wideband digital receivers, high-sensitivity antennas, and advanced signal processing capabilities tailored to the unique operational environment of rotary-wing aircraft, including low-altitude flight profiles and complex electromagnetic landscapes.

