Market Challenges
Complex Signal Environments and Integration Issues – Operating in dense electromagnetic environments poses significant challenges for Radar Warning Receiver (RWR) systems on rotorcraft. Terrain masking, clutter, and signal interference can complicate accurate threat detection and localization for helicopter platforms during low-level flights.
High Development and Integration Costs – Advanced RWR systems require substantial investment in research, testing, and platform-specific integration, which can strain procurement budgets for certain defense programs.
Rapidly Evolving Threat Landscapes – Adversaries continuously develop new radar technologies and electronic countermeasures, requiring frequent upgrades to maintain effectiveness of existing RWR installations on rotorcraft fleets.

